[A.]
<h2>Supercalifradgjyalisticexpeolodocious</h2>
<i>"4 on 1's are not fun"<br>
-Mike</i>
<p>Keep these points in mind:
<p>~B~E~r1.~lYou got all 4 workshops under fire from a crossbow and 3 manowars.
<p>~B~E~r2.~lYour only defense for them is one ice tower and two whiriligig bases each.
<p>~B~E~r3.~lYou got all the tech, but sun barricades wont be able to save your workshops.
<p>~B~E~r4.~lYour temple isn't going to be in any real danger at the start.

$Button=More,Tell,More

[More]
<h2>~B~wBlah blah blah...</h2>
<p>~B~E~i      Ok, at first glance this map appears to be a very familiar setup, and basically it is, I know almost everyone comes up with this idea for a map at one time or another, but these kinds of maps are fun. You and the ais are as close as possible - the map is basically built for speed.  I generally try to stay away from ais that are way on the other end of the map.  In my opinion that makes the map a lot less fun.  Anyway, I tried my best to make it as original as I could. So hey enjoy it.
<br>                                                     -Mike Byrne aka Australian_Dingo
$Button=Thanks,Tell,More2

[More2]
<p>~B~l*Remember:~IIt's not whether you win or lose, it's how you play the game.
